From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 14:24:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 80/85] media: cedrus: Put the H.264 SPS timing fields in order

num_units_in_tick is the frame period's numerator and time_scale twice
its denominator. They were swapped, so a 30 fps stream announced 1/30 fps.
---
 drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_enc_h264.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_enc_h264.c b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_enc_h264.c
index b2cc3ca..391fda5 100644
--- a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_enc_h264.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_enc_h264.c
@@ -948,11 +948,11 @@ static void cedrus_enc_h264_job_configure_sps(struct cedrus_context *cedrus_ctx)
 	cedrus_enc_h264_coded_bit(dev, 1);
 
 	/* Syntax element: num_units_in_tick. */
-	cedrus_enc_h264_coded_u32(dev, timeperframe->denominator);
+	cedrus_enc_h264_coded_u32(dev, timeperframe->numerator);
 
 	/* A frame requires two ticks in H.264. */
 	/* Syntax element: time_scale. */
-	cedrus_enc_h264_coded_u32(dev, timeperframe->numerator * 2);
+	cedrus_enc_h264_coded_u32(dev, timeperframe->denominator * 2);
 
 	/* Syntax element: fixed_frame_rate_flag. */
 	cedrus_enc_h264_coded_bit(dev, 1);
-- 
